\]
\[
2^{68} \equiv 38^2 \mod 289 \equiv -1 \mod 289
\]
Then:
\[
2^{136} \equiv (-1)^2 \equiv 1 \mod 289
\]
Thus, the smallest \(k\) such that \(2^k \equiv 1 \mod 289\) is 136. Therefore, the order of \(\bar{2}\) in \(\mathbb{Z}_{289}^\times\) is \(\boxed{136}\).<|im_end|>
