   - **Central Circle**: 1 circle at the center of the large circle.
   - **First Surrounding Layer (Layer 1)**: This layer forms a ring of circles around the central circle. The distance from the center to the centers of these circles must be at least \(\pi/2\) (twice the radius of the small circles) to prevent overlap. The radius required for Layer 1 is \(\pi/2\). This layer can hold 6 circles, forming a regular hexagon.

2. **Second Surrounding Layer (Layer 2) Consideration**:
